@startuml recovery-sequence
!include _theme.puml
autonumber "<b>0"
participant "Station" as S
participant "Driver\n(AVPlayer / ExoPlayer)" as D
participant "PlaybackEngine" as E #EEF4FC
participant "Runtime\n(network monitor)" as N
participant "JS" as J

S -> D : audio
D -> E : playing
E -> J : status: playing
== Wi-Fi drops ==
N -> E : network offline
note right of E: detection turns eager\n(networkSuspectMs 20 s)
D -> E : buffering (buffer drained)
E -> E : no buffer progress 3 s\n→ socket is dead
E -> J : status: reconnecting\nattempt 1 · offline probe
...offline: attempts are skipped, every third runs as a probe...
N -> E : network online (restore edge)
E -> E : reset backoff
E -> D : open(gen + 1)\nat the live edge
D -> S : new connection
S -> D : audio
D -> E : playing (gen + 1)
E -> J : status: playing
note over D, E: Events from the old generation are dropped:\na late "failed" from the dead item cannot undo the recovery.
note over J: JS only mirrors. With JS frozen in the background,\nsteps 4–14 happen exactly the same.
@enduml
